ents are *not* about putting all your eggs in one basket—they're about giving you a smarter, more responsive basket. You can still carry a backup card or a small amount of cash for emergencies, just like you might carry a spare tire in your car. But for day-to-day reliability, the ability to monitor, freeze, and manage your money in real time from your phone is a level of control that cash and cards simply cannot match. Ultimately, reliability isn't just about avoiding failure—it's about how quickly and easily you can recover when something goes wrong. And on that front, mobile payments win hands down.
